From 41357914c8ea0455c76d0099e18f61cece97cce3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TWL Build <build@twl.local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:55:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(messaging): a button that says whether SMS and email
 actually work
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The last four messaging failures were configuration, not code: no key, an unapproved
sender ID, the wrong route, an empty wallet — and every one of them was discovered by
registering a test account and waiting, or by reading a server log the owner of the
business should not have to read.

Admin -> Settings -> Messaging now shows both drivers and their real state, and sends
one real message on demand. The result panel prints the provider's own sentence
("Sender ID not found", "Insufficient balance") because "Termii responded 200" is not
an explanation — Termii answers 200 with an error body, which is precisely why the
generic route silently fails to reach DND numbers.

Behind it: DeliveryResult carries providerStatus and providerMessage (truncated, never
the key), summariseProviderReply() turns a provider body into the one sentence worth
showing, and MessagingService.status() reports readiness per channel without ever
reading a secret out loud.

documentation/SMS-SETUP.md writes down what "turning SMS on" actually requires — sender
ID approval, DND route activation, per-message cost — and what each provider error means.

5 new tests (123 total), typecheck and production build clean.
