From bbcb11ba76ffd79e9599536f81d8eb1c0686b4de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TWL Build <build@twl.local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:05:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(auth): stop offering phone confirmation that cannot
 happen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phone confirmation is optional — booking needs an email address, not a handset — but a
deployment with no SMS provider was still advertising it: a "Verify now" link on the
settings page, a permanent "Your phone number is not verified" banner nobody could
clear, and, on the verification screen itself, a code box under the words "we sent you
a 6-digit code".

Outside production the API hands the code back and shows it on screen, so the flow
completes honestly. In production it does not, so that screen was a dead end with a
false statement on top of it.

Now the API refuses the request out loud when there is no driver and no code to show
(503 SMS_UNAVAILABLE, "nothing was sent"), and the browser reads the public health
block — which has always said whether SMS is really configured — to decide what to
offer: the settings row reads "Not confirmed" instead of a link that cannot work, the
banner stays quiet, and step 2 of verification explains in two sentences that the step
is off and unneeded. The customer home badge reads "Phone on file" rather than a
warning that will never clear.

2 new tests (125 total), typecheck and production build clean.
